ect hardcoded `/tmp` paths in test helpers\n2. Database fixtures or helper methods that create Run records with `/tmp` target_root values\n\n## Affected Test Files\nPrimary failure point:\n- `spec/integration/mcp_workflows_spec.rb` → `create_run()` helper (line 366)\n\nSecondary failure pattern:\n- `spec/services/mcp_tools/*.rb` → Uses same workspace creation pattern\n- `spec/system/*.rb` → Database fixtures create Run records with /tmp paths\n\n## Verification Evidence\n```\n$ echo $TMPDIR\n/tmp/claude-501\n\n$ ls -ld $TMPDIR\ndrwx------@ 1154 stockn  wheel  36928 Jul 24 23:04 /tmp/claude-501\n\n$ touch $TMPDIR/test-write: ✓ SUCCESS\n$ touch /tmp/test-write: ✗ EPERM\n```\n\n## Reproduction Command\n```bash\ncd /Users/stockn/Source/workflow-orchestrator/when-launching-a-task-we-should-be-able-to-add-a-4780\nbundle exec rspec spec/integration/mcp_workflows_spec.rb:4\n```\n\n## Implementation Boundary\nThe fix requires identifying all locations where test infrastructure hardcodes `/tmp` and replacing with environment-aware temporary directory selection:\n- `create_run()` helper in `spec/integration/mcp_workflows_spec.rb`\n- Similar helpers in other test files\n- Any fixtures or factory patterns that create Run records with hardcoded paths\n- Database seeds that reference /tmp for target_root or workspace.root_path\n\n## Notes\nThis is a test infrastructure issue, not an application logic failure. The application itself may be correct; the test environment constraints require the test helpers to adapt to sandbox write restrictions.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d2892c6-77f9-4067-a6e3-5a7da84f2051","uuid":"70662896-cc53-4c1d-91f6-27338cb10497","timestamp":"2026-07-24T21:04:42.936Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Initial Diagnosis: Test Infrastructure Permission Failures\n\n## Summary\nIntegration tests are failing with `Errno::EPERM: Operation not permitted` when creating temporary workspace directories. The root cause is hardcoded `/tmp`